WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.400
Universes collide in more ways than one in the new&nbsp;
"Spider-Verse" movie – and it definitely doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:10.295
happen the way you might expect. Warning: spoilers&nbsp;
ahead for "Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse."

00:00:10.295 --> 00:00:14.520
Seeing as how the "Spider-Verse" follow-up&nbsp;
originally had a "Part One" as part of its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:18.060
title, it's no surprise it ends by&nbsp;
setting up another sequel. But the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.701
film has wide-ranging implications for the&nbsp;
future of other Spider-Man projects, too.

00:00:22.701 --> 00:00:25.980
The movie contains many references&nbsp;
to Spider-Man projects of the past,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:31.560
both hand-drawn and live-action. Viewers also&nbsp;
get to see clips – but not new material – from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:35.880
Tobey Maguire and Andrew Garfield's versions&nbsp;
of the character. There's even a moment where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:40.414
The Spot travels to the "Venom" universe,&nbsp;
speaking to Mrs. Chen for a little bit.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:41.820
"So?"

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:46.080
However, arguably one of the best surprises&nbsp;
from the film is when Miles gets a tour of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:51.660
Spider-Man 2099's compound and gets taken to&nbsp;
an area housing classic Spider-Man villains who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:54.960
ended up in the wrong universe. There&nbsp;
are many great gags in this sequence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:59.640
including a moose version of Mysterio, but&nbsp;
fans will likely be most taken with a surprise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:04.800
cameo from Donald Glover as a live-action&nbsp;
version of Prowler, complete with costume.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.460
While this version of Prowler could have&nbsp;
come from anywhere in the multiverse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:13.380
fans won't forget that Glover already played&nbsp;
Prowler alter ego Aaron Davis in "Spider-Man:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:17.160
Homecoming." A lot of time has&nbsp;
passed between that movie and now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:21.840
so it's possible he went from a low-level&nbsp;
criminal to a full-on supervillain, suggesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.020
a viable path for the next live-action&nbsp;
movie with Tom Holland's Spider-Man.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:30.720
"Spider-Man" producer Amy Pascal recently hinted&nbsp;
that a live-action Miles Morales project is in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.980
works. Without further details, it's impossible&nbsp;
to say whether this would be part of the Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:39.660
Cinematic Universe or something separate within&nbsp;
Sony's wheelhouse, but Donald Glover's cameo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:43.740
in "Across the Spider-Verse" could hint&nbsp;
at a storyline coming within the MCU..

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:48.120
Pascal also revealed that "Spider-Man&nbsp;
4" with Tom Holland is in the pipeline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:51.561
so it's possible Miles and Aaron could&nbsp;
have a story together in that film.

00:01:51.561 --> 00:01:54.683
"I don't want those weapons in this&nbsp;
neighborhood. I got a nephew who live here."

00:01:54.683 --> 00:01:58.957
While Holland's Peter Parker would likely have&nbsp;
a larger adversary to deal with, Glover's Uncle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.957 --> 00:02:03.360
Aaron could factor into the story somehow,&nbsp;
bringing Peter and Miles into contact with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:08.100
one another. If Marvel wanted to keep the focus on&nbsp;
Peter Parker, it's possible Miles and Aaron would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:12.540
only play smaller roles, with Miles getting bit&nbsp;
by the spider and facing the death of his uncle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:17.580
in his own standalone film. Or we could see Miles&nbsp;
undergo the beginnings of his character arc in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:22.260
"Spider-Man 4" before spinning off into another&nbsp;
movie, similarly to how Tom Holland initially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:26.686
came onto the scene in "Captain America: Civil&nbsp;
War" before appearing in his first solo movie.

00:02:26.686 --> 00:02:30.540
Then again, Glover's appearance in "Across&nbsp;
the Spider-Verse" may just function as a bit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:35.160
of fan service and nothing more. More details&nbsp;
on "Spider-Man 4" and beyond probably won't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:39.693
materialize until after the writers' strike&nbsp;
is over, so for now, fans can only speculate.

00:02:39.693 --> 00:02:43.833
"And that's when the world went crazy."

00:02:43.833 --> 00:02:46.380
Donald Glover has an intriguing&nbsp;
history with Spider-Man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:51.060
and even partly inspired the creation&nbsp;
of Miles Morales. So him popping up in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.434
"Across the Spider-Verse" is a great&nbsp;
cameo for more reasons than one.

00:02:54.434 --> 00:02:57.720
When the "Spider-Man" film franchise was&nbsp;
being rebooted with "The Amazing Spider-Man,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:01.260
Glover half-jokingly campaigned&nbsp;
to snag the role of Peter Parker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:04.668
even showing up with Spider-Man&nbsp;
pajamas in an episode of "Community."

00:03:04.668 --> 00:03:09.600
The role ultimately went to Andrew Garfield, but&nbsp;
Glover did something arguably even more important.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:14.340
Brian Michael Bendis and artist Sara Pichelli&nbsp;
were working on the "Ultimate Spider-Man" comic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:19.258
when Glover inspired them to really create a&nbsp;
Black Spider-Man. Bendis even told USA Today,

00:03:19.258 --> 00:03:20.760
"I saw him in the costume and thought,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.700
'I would like to read that book.' So&nbsp;
I was glad I was writing that book."

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:29.029
Glover even voiced Miles for two episodes of&nbsp;
2015's "Ultimate Spider-Man" cartoon. As such,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.029 --> 00:03:33.371
it was appropriate casting to bring him&nbsp;
into the MCU as Miles' uncle, Aaron.

00:03:33.371 --> 00:03:37.140
The creative team behind "Spider-Man: Far&nbsp;
From Home" even considered bringing Glover&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:41.700
back for a brief role, but it just didn't pan&nbsp;
out. Fortunately, Glover's cameo in "Across&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:46.140
the Spider-Verse" suggests the character could&nbsp;
still be out there, and if there's anyone who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:50.868
should help usher Miles Morales into a live-action&nbsp;
setting, it should definitely be Donald Glover.

